{"author":{"id":"89da5fec8eff6d69dbcdd68f81be7e9163b16f34b17e978ecf3554487379f453"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1772907476,"nonce":"r9nJGRg8vNXM5LqeW83cKRP4mGM=","message":"**Debugging trajectory**\n\n**Attempt 1** (migration 24, f2f1f8e): Added `backfillProjectRepoNames()` to db.ts. The function joined `session_projects` with `sessions` WHERE `cwd LIKE '%/worktrees/%'`. Intent was: if the session was running from a worktree path, extract the repo root from it.\n\n**Why it failed**: Sessions store the *repo root* as `cwd` (e.g. `/Users/mll/.dotfiles`), not the worktree path (e.g. `/Users/mll/.dotfiles/worktrees/feature__foo`). The join found zero rows. Migration ran (schema version advanced to 24) but no data was updated.\n\n**Discovered via**: Querying the live DB after merge: `SELECT repo_id, cwd FROM session_projects JOIN sessions ON session_id = id WHERE repo_id LIKE 'feature%' LIMIT 5` — all `cwd` values were repo roots, none contained `/worktrees/`.\n\n**Attempt 2** (migration 25, current branch `feature/issue-fetch-and-backfill-fix`): `backfillProjectRepoNamesV2()` uses the correct approach — derives repo name from `path.basename(cwd).replace(/^\\.+/, '')`. This maps `/Users/mll/.dotfiles` → `dotfiles`, `/Users/mll/Main/15 WWW/mll.bio` → `mll.bio`, etc. Rows where `cwd` produces the same value as the existing `repo_id` are skipped.","files":null}]}